<Layout
	title="The Knowledge Base"
	description="Education at Punk Positronics: The Manual is live now. Masterclasses and Build-Days launch when the waitlist says so — Phase 2, honored."
	pubDate={new Date()}
	heroImage="/og-default.png"
>
	<h1>The Knowledge Base</h1>
	<p>
		Sovereignty isn't just about tools; it's about knowledge. We turn the struggle of implementation into a roadmap for others — but on a schedule that respects reality, not a brochure.
	</p>

	<h2 class="resource">The Manual <span class="flag">Live Now</span></h2>
	<p>
		Beyond simple SOPs: the <a href="/manual">Open Ops Manual</a> is a blueprint for business resilience. We document the work already in progress — the wins, the failures, the compromises — public by default. Designed to enable the Succession Protocol: the business as a community-resilient asset, maintainable by the community, with no single point of failure called "the man."
	</p>

	<h2 class="resource">Masterclasses <span class="flag">Phase 2</span></h2>
	<p>
		Video step-by-steps for FOSS tool implementation — from Linux Mint desktops to Proxmox homesteads. Honest status: parked until there's a waitlist. Education is exhaust, not a workstream — it comes from documenting work already being done.
	</p>

	<h2 class="resource">Build-Days <span class="flag">Phase 2</span></h2>
	<p>
		Small-group physical workshops for home-lab setup and device reclamation — Kids' Tech Lockdown days, phone-reclamation benches, NAS builds. Also parked until the waitlist says otherwise. When they launch, they'll be announced on <a href="https://punkpositronics.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Punk Pages</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 class="resource">The FOSS Sovereignty Catalog <span class="flag">Live Now</span></h2>
	<p>
		The knowledge distribution that exists today: a curated, community-validated menu of open-source tools that replace predatory SaaS, tiered by the Sovereignty Maturity Model. <a href="/catalog">Read the Catalog</a> — it's the same menu we hand clients during Cloud Exit Audits.
	</p>
</Layout>